    "dealing": "The deal is counter-clockwise, starting with the dealer. Each player receives four cards. In the English reconstruction, two cards are dealt to each player, then a betting phase, then two more cards each; in the Spanish version the four cards may be dealt one by one. The deck is typically 40 cards (Italian or Spanish strip); the Roman version uses the full 52-card pack.",
